extends layouts/main

block content
  h1.page-title Privacy notice
  section.card.card-pad
    p The SLU OJT Portal keeps the records needed to monitor your on-the-job training (OJT). Your personal data is handled under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173).

    h2.section-title What we collect
    ul
      li Interns: name, student ID, course, year, class code, SLU email, chosen company, and the files you submit (requirements, weekly reports and journals).
      li Advisers and department heads: name, SLU email and department.
      li For security: sign-in times, IP addresses and failed login attempts.

    h2.section-title Why we collect it
    ul
      li To review your requirements, hours and reports, and to approve your deployment.
      li To protect accounts, for example by locking an account after 5 wrong passwords.

    h2.section-title Who can see it
    p Your OJT adviser, your department head, and the staff who maintain the portal. Your data is not sold or shared outside SLU.

    h2.section-title Cookies
    p The portal uses one cookie to keep you logged in. It does not use tracking or advertising cookies.

    h2.section-title How long we keep it
    p Records are kept for as long as SLU's records policy requires.

    h2.section-title Your rights
    p You can ask to see, correct or delete your data. Contact your OJT adviser or the SLU Data Protection Officer.
